WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.260
In Battersea Park, London,
stands a Peace Pagoda.

2
00:00:04.310 --> 00:00:07.400
The monks who built it
walk and drum for peace,

3
00:00:07.450 --> 00:00:10.690
chanting one phrase again and again.

4
00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:13.500
That phrase is the title
of a Buddhist text,

5
00:00:13.550 --> 00:00:17.040
the Lotus Sutra, with a word of devotion.

6
00:00:17.090 --> 00:00:22.200
A Japanese monk, Nichiren, believed
Japan had entered an age of decline,

7
00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:26.100
when older practices no longer
lead people to awakening.

8
00:00:26.150 --> 00:00:30.500
But can chanting the title of one
book be the whole of Buddhism?

9
00:00:30.550 --> 00:00:34.100
In this mission, you'll
unpack the chant word by word,

10
00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:36.530
and see how it is practised at home.

11
00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:40.100
Then you'll meet the movements
that carry his teaching today.

12
00:00:40.150 --> 00:00:45.170
Your mission: weigh up whether one chanted
title can be the whole of Buddhism.
